@* The plant's file - export and import (rows 43 and 44) - as a section of the page's strip, the
   first one (owner's decision of 27/9: until then it was a closed box of its own in the band above
   the strip, next to the checks). It is first because it is about the plant as a whole, before
   anything that is done on it; and it is the section nearest to where it used to be.
   <para>
   <b>Opened and shut by the page</b>, in a floating window over the canvas (DrawioWindow, spec
   2026-09-29), open together with any of the other sections: the button of the strip and the
   window's X both ask the page, and the page hands back <see cref="Open"/>. Shut to begin with, as
   it was in the band: one of its two commands replaces the whole plant.
   </para>
   <para>
   <b>The body stays in the page while shut</b>, as Operations' does - and here it is not only a
   matter of size: the import's confirmation is a dialog of ImportExport, and taking the component
   off the page would throw away a file the operator has chosen and not yet confirmed. So a pending
   import survives the window being shut: the hidden window hides its dialog with it (display:none
   hides what is inside, whatever its positioning), nothing can press "Confirm" while it is hidden,
   and the button of the strip says that an import is waiting - opening the window again shows the
   confirmation again. It is never confirmed or cancelled by shutting the window: only "Confirm"
   writes, and only "Cancel" (or a click outside the dialog, as always) throws it away. What it
   compares is not frozen either (fix round of 27/9): the file is compared with the plant again when
   the window is opened again, when the plant the page holds moves, and in any case at "Confirm",
   before anything is written - see ImportExport.OnParametersSetAsync. The button's sentence follows
   it - in its tip and its name for a screen reader, the visible word is "Plant file" - waiting, being
   written, not written, compared again, or not comparable again because the plant could not be read.
   </para>
   ImportExport is rendered only once the page has the plant (<see cref="Graph"/>), as it was when
   the band rendered this box: the page never goes back to no plant, so once rendered it stays. *@
@using Wcs.WebEditor.Drawio.Coordination
@using Wcs.WebEditor.Io
@using Wcs.WebEditor.Model
@using static Wcs.Common.Enums

@* The button of the bar (passata grafica, 2026-09-29): the icon and the name, and while an import is
   waiting a "!" on it - the sentence that says what the import is doing, which used to be the
   button's whole text, is inside it behind a tip (drawio-has-tip: the mouse or the keyboard's focus
   on the button shows it), and is its name for a screen reader. *@
<button type="button" id="drawio-plant-file-toggle" class="drawio-section-toggle drawio-has-tip" aria-label="@SummaryText"
        aria-pressed="@(Open ? "true" : "false")" @onclick="() => OnToggle.InvokeAsync()">
    <DrawioIcon Name="plant-file" />
    <span class="drawio-toggle-label">Plant file</span>
    @if (_pending is not null)
    {
        <span class="drawio-badge" aria-hidden="true">!</span>
        <span class="drawio-tip" role="tooltip">@SummaryText</span>
    }
</button>
@* The paragraph that said what the two commands do opened the window until the passata grafica: it is
   behind the "?" of the title bar now, word for word, and the commands are the window's first line. *@
<DrawioWindow Id="drawio-plant-file" Class="drawio-plant-file" Title="Plant file" Icon="plant-file"
              Open="Open" OnClose="() => OnClose.InvokeAsync()" Place="Place"
              Resizable="false" AutoSize="true" PreferredSize="PlantFileSize">
    <Help>
        <p id="drawio-plant-file-scope" class="drawio-plant-file-scope">
            The export reads the plant from the host - every device with its configuration, the junctions, the
            door maps, the positions, the PLC connections and the free drawing added by hand - into one file.
            The import replaces the whole plant with a file's, all or nothing, and cannot be undone: it asks for
            the edit permit at the confirmation, and says first what it is about to lose. It goes through only
            with the engine stopped (Stop), and not while the plant has missions or rows in the extraction
            queue. A file exported before 2026-09-19 does not carry the free drawing and leaves it alone - the
            confirmation says which kind you chose. A file waiting for its confirmation keeps waiting while this
            section is shut.
        </p>
    </Help>
    <ChildContent>
        <div class="drawio-plant-file-body">
            <div id="drawio-plant-file-commands" class="drawio-plant-file-commands">
                @if (Graph is { } graph)
                {
                    <ImportExport Graph="graph" CanEdit="true" EngineStatus="EngineStatus"
                                  WriteThroughThePage="WriteThroughThePage"
                                  ReloadUrl="/editor/drawio"
                                  Shown="Open"
                                  OnPendingImportChanged="PendingImportChanged" />
                }
                else
                {
                    <span id="drawio-plant-file-loading" class="drawio-plant-file-loading">Loading the plant...</span>
                }
            </div>
        </div>
    </ChildContent>
</DrawioWindow>

@code {
    private static readonly DrawioWindowSize PlantFileSize = new(680, 420);

    /// <summary>Whether the page has this section's window open.</summary>
    [Parameter] public bool Open { get; set; }

    /// <summary>
    /// The button of the strip was pressed: the page opens the window, brings it to the front if it is
    /// open behind another, or shuts it if it is the one in front - and leaves the other windows as they are.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter] public EventCallback OnToggle { get; set; }

    /// <summary>The window's X was pressed, or Esc in it: the page shuts the window, and does nothing if it is already shut.</summary>
    [Parameter] public EventCallback OnClose { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Where the window opens when this browser remembers nothing about it (see DrawioWindowPlace).</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public DrawioWindowPlace Place { get; set; } = null!;

    /// <summary>The plant as the page holds it, null until it is loaded: the commands wait for it.</summary>
    [Parameter] public PlantGraph? Graph { get; set; }

    /// <summary>The engine's state as the page shows it, null when not known (see ImportExport.EngineStatus).</summary>
    [Parameter] public NavigatorStatusTypes? EngineStatus { get; set; }

    /// <summary>The page's own way through for the import's write (see ImportExport.WriteThroughThePage).</summary>
    [Parameter] public Func<Func<Task>, Task<DrawioSaid?>>? WriteThroughThePage { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Where the file waiting in the import's confirmation stands, or null when none is waiting.</summary>
    private PlantImportStatus? _pending;

    /// <summary>What the button of the bar says of the import - in its tip and in its name for a screen reader - so that a shut window still tells what its hidden dialog would.</summary>
    private string SummaryText => _pending switch
    {
        null => "Plant file",
        { Phase: PlantImportPhase.Writing } => $"Plant file (the import of \"{_pending.FileName}\" is being written...)",
        { Phase: PlantImportPhase.NotWritten } => $"Plant file (the import of \"{_pending.FileName}\" was not written - open to see why)",
        { Phase: PlantImportPhase.NotCompared } => $"Plant file (the import of \"{_pending.FileName}\" could not be compared again with the plant - open to see why)",
        { Phase: PlantImportPhase.PlantChanged } => $"Plant file (the plant changed: the import of \"{_pending.FileName}\" has to be confirmed again)",
        _ => $"Plant file (an import is waiting for confirmation: \"{_pending.FileName}\")",
    };

    private void PendingImportChanged(PlantImportStatus? status) => _pending = status;
}
